# Build context exclusions. The single most important entry here is node_modules:
# every image installs its own dependencies inside the target-arch build stage, and
# esbuild/rollup/Prisma all ship per-platform binaries. Letting a macOS arm64
# node_modules leak into the context would either bloat the layer or, worse, shadow
# the container's correct install with host binaries that cannot execute.
node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Build output — every image rebuilds this from source inside the build stage.
dist
**/dist
apps/web/dist

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. .env.example is not matched by these.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.docker.example

# Test and tooling artifacts
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
coverage
**/coverage

# Agent / editor state
.claude
.agents
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Docs and design assets: not needed to build or run any of the three apps.
assets
design_handoff_daleelex_enhancement
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Docker's own files — changing a compose file should not bust the build cache.
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
